<p>Neither the compiler nor the spec defines an HTTP client or server API yet. This page invents no function names; the spec fixes only how network access is declared, checked and tested.</p>

<h2 id="get">Send a GET request and read the body</h2>
<p><strong>Not in the standard library yet.</strong> There is no client call; three spec rules will apply: any socket access is the <code>net</code> effect (§14), so a request function says <code>uses net</code> and the package lists <code>.net</code> in <code>capabilities</code> in <code>package.byn</code>; third-party API responses are <code>Untrusted&lt;T&gt;</code> (§15.1), so build a type with <code>requires</code> rules from the body before trusting it; an outbound target is checked against a host allowlist under <code>net</code> (§15.1).</p>
<p><code>Io.run</code> can start an external tool with an argument vector and no shell. This needs the network, so the page does not run it, but it passes <code>bayan check</code>:</p>
<pre><code class="byn">void main() fails IoError {
    let args: string[2] = ["-s", "https://example.com/"]
    let r = try Io.run("curl", args.span)
    print(r.stdout)
}</code></pre>
<pre><code class="other" data-lang="Python">body = requests.get("https://example.com/").text</code></pre>

<h2 id="post">Send a POST request with a JSON body and headers</h2>
<p><strong>Not in the standard library yet.</strong> The spec names <code>@derive(Json)</code> and <code>T.fromJson(…)</code> for JSON, and header values use a <code>HeaderValue</code> type that refuses control characters (§15.1). Derivations are "not in v0.1" (§5.3), and there is no request API, so nothing runs.</p>

<h2 id="server">Run an HTTP server and route paths</h2>
<p><strong>Not in the standard library yet.</strong> The spec mentions server pieces without defining one: handlers are ordinary functions that can fail (<code>Response handle(Request r) fails DbError</code>, §8); <code>@status(400)</code> maps an error variant to an HTTP status (§8); each request gets its own arena capped at 16 MiB (§9); route discovery uses a <code>comptime</code> query, <code>Program.functionsWith&lt;HttpRoute&gt;()</code> (§12.5, "Not in v0.1"). Request query, body, headers, cookies and route parameters are all <code>Untrusted&lt;T&gt;</code>.</p>
<pre><code class="other" data-lang="Go">http.HandleFunc("/hello", func(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
    fmt.Fprintln(w, "hello")
})
http.ListenAndServe(":8080", nil)</code></pre>
